  "id": "devaluation",
  "term": "devaluation",
  "definition": "Devaluation is the experience or expectation that a person’s language or language variety will be treated as less valuable, less authoritative, or less acceptable in a given social setting. In this context, it reflects how broader social hierarchies and norms can lower speakers’ expected recognition, belonging, self-worth, and participation.",
